<title>GERMANY: Germany details revised 1995, H1 1996 trade data.</title>
<headline>Germany details revised 1995, H1 1996 trade data.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office published the following details on revised import, export and trade totals for 1995 and the first half of 1996. All figures in billion of marks.</p>
<p>			   TRADE SURPLUS     EXPORTS	IMPORTS</p>
<p> JAN-JUNE 1996	  42.496	     381.773	339.277</p>
<p>  January		  4.619		61.341	 56.722</p>
<p>  February		 8.392		62.878	 54.486</p>
<p>  March		    6.183		65.062	 58.879</p>
<p>  April		    7.648		65.282	 57.634</p>
<p>  May			9.169		64.519	 55.350</p>
<p>  June		     6.485		62.691	 56.206</p>
<p> FULL YEAR 1995	 85.303	     749.465	664.162</p>
<p>  January		  8.337		58.459	 50.122</p>
<p>  February		 5.774		59.614	 53.840</p>
<p>  March		    4.905		66.663	 61.758</p>
<p>  April		    6.140		58.381	 52.241</p>
<p>  May			8.261		64.534	 56.273</p>
<p>  June		     8.172		65.884	 57.712</p>
<p>  July		     5.092		59.174	 54.082</p>
<p>  August		   6.895		56.878	 49.983</p>
<p>  September		7.650		63.834	 56.184</p>
<p>  October		  7.741		65.674	 57.933</p>
<p>  November		 9.968		66.958	 56.990</p>
<p>  December		 6.368		63.412	 57.044</p>
<p>NOTE -- The Statistics Office said the figures are not seasonally-adjusted. Figures for 1995 are final, but those for the first half of 1996 are preliminary and subject to later revision. -- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
